Subject: [PATCH] vrend: VideoToolbox backend for the virgl video interface (macOS)

Hardware video decode for macOS hosts behind the guest's VA-API driver:
virgl_video_vt.m implements virgl_video.h on VideoToolbox (H.264 decode),
rebuilding SPS/PPS from the stateless descriptors and learning the PPS
reference-index defaults from slice headers.  Decoded pictures are
IOSurface-backed; vrend binds each plane as a rectangle texture and blits
it into the guest's plane resources, fenced so the picture returns to the
decoder's pool only after the GPU has read it.  Planar (IYUV/YV12) targets
go through a VTPixelTransferSession.  Video is offered only when the
backend initialised (vrend_state.video_available), and on darwin the video
build needs neither libdrm, EGL nor libva.
---
